<decompilertest>
<binaryimage arch="x86:LE:64:default:gcc">
<!--
    kuna `tailform`, the no-return form: in a statement list that ends in a
    call that does not return, `if (c) { X } T..; f();`, where `X` leaves (a
    return of any value, statements and a return, a jump), prints as
    `if (!c) { T..; f(); } X`.  Neither path reaches the end of the list, so
    `X` still runs only when `c` holds; authors write the fatal arm as the
    `if` body (`if (n < 0) xalloc_die(); return n;`), while the binary's
    layout often leaves it as the function's trailing statement.

    Stage / sub-stage: P8 "goto-quality", a print-tree edit after final
    structuring, part of `option tailform` (no threshold applies).

    The image is decompiler/crates/kuna-analysis/tests/fixtures/
    tailnoret_gcc_O2_x86_64 (tailnoret.c, gcc 11.4 -O2
    -fno-reorder-blocks-and-partition), loaded whole so `abort` and `exit`
    are known not to return: scaled (a two-statement fatal arm before
    `return r + 7;`), pick (two fatal tests the compiler merged), lookup (the
    fatal test after a loop) and store (a void function whose other arm is a
    store and a `return;`).

    Pass 1 runs with `option tailform off` and prints the binary's form: the
    valued return inside the `if`, the fatal call last.  Pass 2 (`option
    tailform on`; the default `model` prints these four the same) prints the
    fatal arm as the `if` body and the return after it.
-->
<bytechunk space="ram" offset="0x100000" readonly="true">c3</bytechunk>
<symbol space="ram" offset="0x100000" name="harness_stub"/>
</binaryimage>
<script>
  <com>clear architecture</com>
  <com>load file decompiler/crates/kuna-analysis/tests/fixtures/tailnoret_gcc_O2_x86_64</com>
  <com>read symbols</com>
  <com>option truthycond on</com>
  <!-- loopcondhoist (default on) makes lookup's head test its loop condition and
       keeps the fatal test inside the loop; kept off so the tail if is checked. -->
  <com>option loopcondhoist off</com>
  <com>option tailform off</com>
  <com>load function scaled</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>load function pick</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>load function lookup</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>load function store</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>option tailform on</com>
  <com>load function scaled</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>load function pick</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>load function lookup</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>load function store</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
</script>
<stringmatch name="tailform no-return #1: off, scaled returns inside the if and ends in exit" min="1" max="1">^  if \(v2\)$
^    return v2 \+ 7;$</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="tailform no-return #2: on, scaled's two-statement fatal arm is the if body" min="1" max="1">^  if \(!v2\) \{$
^    __fprintf_chk\(.*$
^    exit\(2\);.*$
^  \}$
^  return v2 \+ 7;$</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="tailform no-return #3: on, pick tests the merged fatal condition and returns after it" min="1" max="1">^  if \(\(!a0\) \|\| \(a1 &gt;= a2\)\)$
^    abort\(\);.*$
^  return a0\[a1\];$</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="tailform no-return #4: on, the fatal test after lookup's loop is the if body" min="1" max="1">^  if \(0 &gt; \(\(int4 \*\)a0\)\[3\]\)$
^    abort\(\);.*$
^  return \(\(int4 \*\)a0\)\[3\];$</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="tailform no-return #5: off, store's store and return are the if body" min="1" max="1">^  if \(a0\) \{$
^    \*a0 = a1;$
^    return;$</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="tailform no-return #6: on, store tests the fatal arm and stores after it" min="1" max="1">^  if \(!a0\)$
^    abort\(\);.*$
^  \*a0 = a1;$
^}</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="tailform no-return #7: every call to abort and exit is printed in both passes" min="8" max="8">^ *(abort|exit)\(.*\);</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="tailform no-return #8: off, pick returns inside the if and abort ends it" min="1" max="1">^  if \(\(a0\) &amp;&amp; \(a1 &lt; a2\)\)$
^    return a0\[a1\];$
^  abort\(\);</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="tailform no-return #9: off, lookup returns inside the if after its loop and abort ends it" min="1" max="1">^  if \(0 &lt;= \(\(int4 \*\)a0\)\[3\]\)$
^    return \(\(int4 \*\)a0\)\[3\];$
^  abort\(\);</stringmatch>
</decompilertest>
